"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nI visited this place to have dinner near Seoul Station.  \nThere weren't as many places to eat around Seoul Station as I expected, so it took some effort to find one.  \n\nBecause the weather was hot and humid, we looked for a place where we could eat indoors without going too far outside, which narrowed our options even further.  \nStill, we found a tonkatsu place that looked like the most solid and reliable choice.  \n\nLocated in the Seoul Station food court, it was popular enough to have a waiting line.  \n\nFortunately, there was only one party ahead of us, so right after registering on the waitlist, we were able to enter without much delay.  \n\nThe ordering system involved scanning a QR code on the table, and paying at the counter upon leaving.  \nAfter much deliberation, we ordered the Curry Katsu Set and the Rosu Katsu Set.  \n\nThe food was served quickly after ordering.  \n\nPerhaps because I usually like curry, I enjoyed the Curry Katsu very much.  \nI did feel a slight pity that there wasn't a bit more curry so I could eat it with the rice as well.  \nThere was an option to add extra curry on the menu, which in hindsight would have been great to order.  \n\nThe Rosu Katsu had some fatty parts since it is pork loin, so it was slightly greasy.  \nIf you can't eat greasy food well, Hire Katsu would probably be better.  \n\nOverall, it was a relatively solid and enjoyable meal.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"